sequenceDiagram
    title Diagram 1: Handling one HTTP request (FIFO) - main critical path
    actor C as Client
    participant M as Master thread
    participant B as Request buffer<br/>(bounded queue + mutex)
    participant W as Worker thread

    C->>+M: connect + "GET /page HTTP/1.0"
    M->>M: accept() -> conn_fd, record t_arrive
    M->>+B: lock(mutex)
    B-->>-M: lock acquired
    M->>+B: put(conn_fd, t_arrive), count++
    B--)W: signal(not_empty)
    M->>B: unlock(mutex)
    deactivate B
    Note over M: Master never reads the request.<br/>It goes straight back to accept().
    deactivate M

    W->>+B: lock(mutex), get() oldest request
    B-->>-W: conn_fd, t_arrive (count--)
    activate W
    W--)B: signal(not_full), unlock(mutex)
    W->>W: record t_dequeue
    W->>C: read request line + headers
    C-->>W: request text
    W->>W: parse request, build response
    W->>C: write "HTTP/1.0 200 OK" + headers + body
    W->>C: close(conn_fd)
    W->>W: record t_done (latency = t_done - t_arrive)
    deactivate W
    Note over W: Worker loops back and waits for the next request
